= Cognition — Simple =

'''Cognition''' means the mental processes people and other organisms use to deal with information.

It includes things such as seeing and recognizing objects, paying [[Attention/Simple|attention]], remembering, [[Learning/Simple|learning]], solving problems, using language, and making decisions.

Cognition is not the same thing as intelligence. Intelligence is one way of talking about how well some abilities work; cognition includes the processes themselves.

Cognition is also not always conscious. Some information can affect what we do even when we are not actively thinking about it.

Scientists study cognition in the brain, in behavior, and sometimes in larger systems that include bodies, tools, and other people.

